As of 2024-2025, Pokémon remains one of the highest-grossing media franchises globally. Recent major releases include Pokémon Scarlet and Violet (Gen IX, 2022, 26+ million units sold), Pokémon Legends: Arceus (2021, 6.5+ million units), and upcoming Pokémon Legends: Z-A (October 2025). The franchise expanded to Pokémon Works (joint venture with ILCA) developing Pokémon Champions (multi-platform turn-based strategy). Pokémon Go remains active. The Trading Card Game has also resurged in popularity. The franchise includes a massive media empire spanning video games, anime (30+ years running), trading cards, movies, and merchandise across all age groups, though primarily targeting ages 5-12.